    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d477">

                <pb facs="0462" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363/855a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ford</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-20T19:00:00-04:00">May 20, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>316. To William Campbell from Marcel Wagner. The number of this message is 0031.
                    We have learned from the Iranian Minister at Washington that his Government has
                    requested him to instruct Curtice and Hoover<anchor n="64" xml:id="d477-f1"/>
                    who are now the official representatives of the Government of Iran to examine
                    under his auspices in Washington offers of both companies. The Minister has
                    requested that their recommendations be subsequently telegraphed to him. If you
                    can, cable confirmation. [Wagner.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d477-f1" n="64" xml:id="d477-f1-content">
                <p>A. A. Curtice and Herbert Hoover, Jr., petroleum geologists, had been
                    commissioned by the Iranian Government as petroleum advisers.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
